{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966812,"nonce":"KHLca2H0VxHeoJFxJ85Bpy4/TfM=","title":"Plan for hot-reloading .blinc files. Zyntax's per-function hot_reload is the wrong tool;","message":"**Goal.** Edit a `.blinc` file and see it in the running app, so widget and CSS\niteration is seconds rather than a rebuild.\n\n**Zyntax's `hot_reload` is NOT the mechanism.**\n`ZyntaxRuntime::hot_reload(name, \u0026HirFunction)` swaps ONE function's machine\ncode, keyed by HirId, with version history and `rollback_function`. The caller\nmust already have lowered new source to HIR and know which function changed,\nand it cannot add or remove declarations. A `.blinc` edit usually moves\nsignals, components, FSMs and the view together, so per-function patching\nmeans HIR diffing for little gain. Keep it in mind only for a future\n\"one component changed\" fast path.\n\n**What works instead** (pinned by `crates/blinc_dsl_core/tests/\nhot_reload_contract.rs`):\n\n1. A live `BlincDsl` can `compile_source` again -- the runtime accepts the\n   redefinition -- and the new view is what renders (2 -\u003e 5 nodes in the test).\n2. Signal VALUES survive a recompile and even a fresh instance: the registry is\n   process-global and keyed by name, and a declared default applies only on\n   first mint (b1fddeb0). A reload keeps what the user typed or clicked.\n3. `blinc_app::hot_reload` already has the plumbing: `watch_dir()` (notify,\n   recursive, background thread), an invalidation queue, `REBUILD_PENDING`, and\n   a wake fn that nudges a window parked in `ControlFlow::Wait`. The windowed\n   loop already drains `take_rebuild_pending()`.\n\n**Phase 1 -- the loop (small).** `BlincDsl::recompile_project(entry, root)`:\nre-run `compile_project`, keep the previous program if it fails. Host watches\nthe DSL root, filters invalidations to `.blinc`, recompiles, marks the tree\ndirty. A parse error mid-typing must never kill the app.\n\n**Phase 2 -- idempotent recompiles (the actual work).** `declared_signals`,\n`declared_fsms` and `compiled_stylesheets` all EXTEND per compile, so a reload\naccumulates duplicates and keeps stale entries. They need replacing per compile\n(or keying by module), and `stylesheets_queued_up_to` needs rethinking so an\nedited `style { }` block REPLACES its previous sheet instead of appending a\nsecond copy. Also: does a deleted component disappear from the component\nregistry, and does re-registering an FSM keep its current state?\n\n**Phase 3 -- state preservation.** Signals are done. Check scroll offsets\n(StableNodeId), focus, and the keyed text buffers in `blinc_cn_dsl::bridge`\n(static, so they survive). Policy already settled: a changed default does NOT\noverwrite a live value.\n\n**Phase 4 -- ergonomics.** A `WindowedApp` entry point that wires watch +\nrecompile, and parse errors surfaced in-window rather than only in the log.\n\nSee project multi module blinc plan, gotcha dsl computed binding zero.","files":null}]}